# Conventional Commit messages

When generating or writing a Git commit message, use this format:

```text
type(optional-scope): imperative description
```

- Use one of these types: `build`, `chore`, `ci`, `docs`, `feat`, `fix`, `perf`, `refactor`, `revert`, `style`, or `test`.
- Keep the header at 100 characters or fewer.
- Use a concise, lowercase, imperative description without a trailing period.
- Add a body only when it explains important context that the header cannot.
- Mark breaking changes with `!` before the colon and add a `BREAKING CHANGE:` footer.

Example: `feat(tasks): add optimistic completion`
